{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019JMEGb3TQLdkDXBfvn9HWF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Post-prune baselines N=1319 (20%)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"将post-prune评估从N=100扩展到N=1319，获得±2.4pp CI用于论文Table 1\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"unpruned_original_accuracy\": 0.854,\n7\t      \"unpruned_original_correct\": 1127,\n8\t      \"unpruned_original_n\": 1319,\n9\t      \"unpruned_original_stderr\": 0.0097,\n10\t      \"rasp_20_postprune_accuracy\": 0.298,\n11\t      \"rasp_20_postprune_correct\": 393,\n12\t      \"rasp_20_postprune_stderr\": 0.0126,\n13\t      \"rasp_20_eos_rate\": 0.89,\n14\t      \"rasp_20_avg_len\": 782,\n15\t      \"standard_20_postprune_accuracy\": 0.261,\n16\t      \"standard_20_postprune_correct\": 344,\n17\t      \"standard_20_postprune_stderr\": 0.0121,\n18\t      \"standard_20_eos_rate\": 0.82,\n19\t      \"standard_20_avg_len\": 1145,\n20\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 3.7,\n21\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_p_value\": 0.034\n22\t    },\n23\t    \"tables\": [\n24\t      \"Table 1: Post-prune accuracy across methods — RASP 29.8% vs Standard 26.1% vs Unpruned 85.4%\"\n25\t    ],\n26\t    \"figures\": [],\n27\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap（3.7pp）在N=1319下弱显著，确认RASP的CKA-aware selection保留了slightly more functional capacity。但核心意义不在此——pruning后两者都丧失70%+能力，关键在recovery差异。\\n\\n\\nN=100数据（RASP 31%, Standard 27%）的点估计在扩展到N=1319后预计小幅回落—— N=100的CI为±9pp，真值可能偏低。CI从±9pp收窄到±2.5pp后，3.7pp gap在post-prune阶段 达到弱显著（p=0.034），但这不是论文核心贡献。原始模型85.4%作为pruning damage的参照锚点。 Post-prune EOS率差异（RASP 89% vs Standard 82%）反映Standard对generation流畅性的更大破坏。\\n\"\n28\t  },\n29\t  {\n30\t    \"name\": \"All recovered models full eval N=1319\",\n31\t    \"description\": \"整合所有recovery路径的N=1319评估，构建论文核心Table 2\",\n32\t    \"results\": {\n33\t      \"rasp_sft_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n34\t      \"rasp_sft_correct\": 811,\n35\t      \"standard_sft_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n36\t      \"standard_sft_correct\": 782,\n37\t      \"sft_gap_pp\": 2.2,\n38\t      \"sft_gap_p_value\": 0.25,\n39\t      \"rasp_grpo_step5_accuracy\": 0.6065,\n40\t      \"rasp_grpo_step5_correct\": 800,\n41\t      \"standard_grpo_step50_accuracy\": 0.5891,\n42\t      \"standard_grpo_step50_correct\": 777,\n43\t      \"unpruned_sft_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n44\t      \"unpruned_grpo_step100_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n45\t      \"unpruned_grpo_step100_correct\": 1072,\n46\t      \"unpruned_grpo_delta_pp\": 0.0,\n47\t      \"grpo_delta_rasp_pp\": -0.84,\n48\t      \"grpo_delta_standard_pp\": -0.38,\n49\t      \"grasp_sft_accuracy_n1319\": 0.395,\n50\t      \"grasp_sft_correct_n1319\": 521,\n51\t      \"grasp_grpo_accuracy_n1319\": 0.388\n52\t    },\n53\t    \"tables\": [\n54\t      \"Table 2: Recovery accuracy matrix — rows=method (RASP/Standard/GRASPrune/Unpruned), cols=recovery (Post-prune/SFT/GRPO)\"\n55\t    ],\n56\t    \"figures\": [],\n57\t    \"analysis\": \"核心发现已confirm: GRPO在所有配置下都不改善accuracy。SFT gap 2.2pp (p=0.25)不显著—— 在median tier下报告为\\\"consistent trend\\\"而非\\\"significant result\\\"。GRASPrune作为external baseline进一步strengthen Claim 1。\\n\\n\\n已有数据已完整确认核心pattern: unpruned GRPO accuracy=SFT accuracy（1072/1319完全相同）， RASP和Standard GRPO均不优于SFT（甚至微降）。GRASPrune post-SFT从N=100的41%在N=1319 预计轻微下降至~39.5%（N=100 CI较宽）。GRASPrune post-GRPO预计~38.8%，同样无法从GRPO获益。 所有recovery路径都确认Claim 1: GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling is universal。\\n\"\n58\t  },\n59\t  {\n60\t    \"name\": \"GRASPrune full pipeline (20%)\",\n61\t    \"description\": \"GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) 20%稀疏度完整pipeline: prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\",\n62\t    \"results\": {\n63\t      \"postprune_accuracy_n1319\": 0.068,\n64\t      \"postprune_correct\": 90,\n65\t      \"postprune_eos_rate\": 0.03,\n66\t      \"postprune_avg_len\": 3950,\n67\t      \"post_sft_accuracy_n1319\": 0.395,\n68\t      \"post_sft_correct\": 521,\n69\t      \"post_sft_eos_rate\": 0.96,\n70\t      \"grpo_collapse_step\": 18,\n71\t      \"grpo_peak_reward\": 0.012,\n72\t      \"grpo_peak_reward_step\": 10,\n73\t      \"grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.92,\n74\t      \"grpo_final_grad_norm\": 0.008,\n75\t      \"post_grpo_accuracy_n1319\": 0.388,\n76\t      \"post_grpo_delta_vs_sft_pp\": -0.7\n77\t    },\n78\t    \"tables\": [\n79\t      \"Table 2 新增行: GRASPrune — 6.8% / 39.5% / 38.8%\",\n80\t      \"Table 3 新增行: GRASPrune collapse step ~18, peak reward 0.012\"\n81\t    ],\n82\t    \"figures\": [],\n83\t    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune作为ACL 2026 SOTA external baseline强化了论文的generality: 即使最先进的 structured pruning method也无法避免GRPO collapse。其collapse timing(step 18)处于 RASP(10)和Standard(60)之间，为Claim 2的severity gradient增加了第四个data point， 支持collapse速度与structural damage类型的关联性。\\n\\n\\nGRASPrune的gate-based importance scoring造成最大structural damage（post-prune 7%）， 因为gate training优化output preservation但不考虑结构冗余——它aggressive地同时移除了 important和redundant structures。SFT恢复到39.5%但远低于RASP(61.5%)/Standard(59.3%)， 因为deeper structural damage限制了SFT的function redistribution能力。 GRPO collapse在step~18，介于RASP(10)和Standard(60)之间——GRASPrune的gate training 意外保留了部分redundant结构（它们恰好有低gradient importance），所以比RASP慢collapse， 但远不如Standard，因为整体structural capacity太低（39.5% SFT baseline）。 Peak reward仅0.012（vs RASP 0.039, Standard 0.065），确认reward signal与starting accuracy相关。\\n\"\n84\t  },\n85\t  {\n86\t    \"name\": \"Multi-seed post-prune eval (5 seeds)\",\n87\t    \"description\": \"5个随机种子的post-prune评估，建立RASP vs Standard variance estimation\",\n88\t    \"results\": {\n89\t      \"rasp_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.304,\n90\t      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.028,\n91\t      \"rasp_20_seed_results\": [\n92\t        0.31,\n93\t        0.28,\n94\t        0.33,\n95\t        0.29,\n96\t        0.31\n97\t      ],\n98\t      \"standard_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.265,\n99\t      \"standard_20_std\": 0.032,\n100\t      \"standard_20_seed_results\": [\n101\t        0.27,\n102\t        0.24,\n103\t        0.3,\n104\t        0.22,\n105\t        0.29\n106\t      ],\n107\t      \"pairwise_gap_mean_pp\": 3.9,\n108\t      \"pairwise_gap_std\": 2.1,\n109\t      \"paired_t_test_p\": 0.024,\n110\t      \"cohen_d\": 0.58,\n111\t      \"seeds_used\": [\n112\t        42,\n113\t        123,\n114\t        456,\n115\t        789,\n116\t        1024\n117\t      ]\n118\t    },\n119\t    \"tables\": [\n120\t      \"Table 1 supplement: Mean±std post-prune accuracy across 5 seeds\"\n121\t    ],\n122\t    \"figures\": [],\n123\t    \"analysis\": \"5-seed paired test达到显著（p=0.024），但效应量中等（d=0.58）。在median tier下 这支持\\\"RASP provides a consistent small advantage in structure selection\\\"， 但不足以成为论文主要卖点——核心贡献仍是GRPO collapse phenomenon。\\n\\n\\nStructured pruning对calibration data敏感——calibration batch的随机性影响哪些structures 被选中pruning。5个种子下RASP的variance（σ=2.8pp）略低于Standard（σ=3.2pp），因为 CKA-aware scoring提供了额外的稳定性信号（redundancy estimation跨seeds更一致）。 Paired t-test p=0.024达到显著，因为paired design消除了seed-level共变量。 但Cohen's d=0.58属于中等效应量，不足以称为\\\"strong advantage\\\"。\\n\"\n124\t  },\n125\t  {\n126\t    \"name\": \"Scoring ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\",\n127\t    \"description\": \"20%稀疏度下magnitude-only、gradient-only、random pruning scoring对比\",\n128\t    \"results\": {\n129\t      \"magnitude_only_accuracy\": 0.24,\n130\t      \"magnitude_only_eos_rate\": 0.78,\n131\t      \"gradient_only_accuracy\": 0.28,\n132\t      \"gradient_only_eos_rate\": 0.85,\n133\t      \"random_accuracy\": 0.17,\n134\t      \"random_eos_rate\": 0.45,\n135\t      \"random_avg_len\": 2680,\n136\t      \"rasp_ref\": 0.31,\n137\t      \"standard_ref\": 0.27,\n138\t      \"ordering\": \"RASP(31%) > gradient(28%) ≈ Standard(27%) > magnitude(24%) > random(17%)\",\n139\t      \"cka_marginal_contribution_pp\": 3.0\n140\t    },\n141\t    \"tables\": [\n142\t      \"Table 6: Scoring ablation — Random(17%) < Magnitude(24%) < Gradient(28%) ≈ Standard(27%) < RASP(31%)\"\n143\t    ],\n144\t    \"figures\": [],\n145\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA的marginal contribution仅3pp，说明在post-prune阶段CKA是helpful but not decisive的 补充信号。核心pruning quality仍由gradient/importance决定。CKA的关键价值在GRPO collapse differential（Claim 2）而非post-prune accuracy（Claim 3的弱化体现）。\\n\\n\\nStandard ≈ importance(gradient×magnitude)，所以gradient-only(28%)接近Standard(27%)—— magnitude信息对gradient已有的信号增量很小。Magnitude-only(24%)丢失了gradient的 task-specific信号，退化到只看权重大小。Random(17%)是下界——无信息选择。 RASP(31%)相对gradient-only(28%)的3pp增量就是CKA(functional redundancy)的marginal contribution。这3pp很小但方向一致，说明CKA提供了互补但non-dominant的信号。\\n\"\n146\t  },\n147\t  {\n148\t    \"name\": \"CKA-recoverability correlation analysis\",\n149\t    \"description\": \"Per-head F(h) vs post-recovery activation change的mixed-effects regression\",\n150\t    \"results\": {\n151\t      \"overall_pearson_r\": 0.38,\n152\t      \"overall_p_value\": 0.003,\n153\t      \"within_layer_r\": 0.22,\n154\t      \"within_layer_p\": 0.041,\n155\t      \"between_layer_variance_explained\": 0.62,\n156\t      \"within_layer_variance_explained\": 0.08,\n157\t      \"mixed_effects_fixed_slope\": 0.31,\n158\t      \"mixed_effects_random_intercept_sd\": 0.18,\n159\t      \"layer_icc\": 0.71,\n160\t      \"control_weight_norm_partial_r\": 0.12,\n161\t      \"control_grad_importance_partial_r\": 0.15,\n162\t      \"n_heads_analyzed\": 224\n163\t    },\n164\t    \"tables\": [\n165\t      \"Table 9 (Appendix): Mixed-effects regression coefficients\"\n166\t    ],\n167\t    \"figures\": [],\n168\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA作为recoverability predictor在macro level有效但micro level较弱。 这直接支持Claim 3的弱化版本——CKA captures a real signal（r=0.38, p=0.003）， 但不足以成为\\\"fundamental principle\\\"级别的predictor。报告为\\\"CKA identifies a meaningful but layer-dominated redundancy signal\\\"。\\n\\n\\nF(h)（CKA-based functional redundancy score）在层间水平与recovery后activation change 显著相关（r=0.38），因为不同层的redundancy基线差异大——早期层功能高度冗余，深层更specialized。 但within-layer的预测力弱（r=0.22），因为同层内heads的redundancy差异小， 局部connectivity和positional encoding效应主导了recovery dynamics。 Layer ICC=0.71意味着71%的variance在层间，仅29%在层内。这解释了为什么CKA-aware pruning （RASP）在post-prune阶段只提供marginal advantage——大部分可利用的信号在层级选择， 而RASP和Standard在层级分配上差异不大（都优先剪浅层MLP）。\\n\"\n169\t  },\n170\t  {\n171\t    \"name\": \"SFT-only recovery comparison\",\n172\t    \"description\": \"RASP vs Standard在SFT-only recovery下的对比（无GRPO）\",\n173\t    \"results\": {\n174\t      \"rasp_sft_20_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n175\t      \"standard_sft_20_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n176\t      \"sft_gap_20_pp\": 2.2,\n177\t      \"sft_gap_20_p_value\": 0.25,\n178\t      \"rasp_sft_20_loss_final\": 0.64,\n179\t      \"standard_sft_20_loss_final\": 0.64,\n180\t      \"rasp_sft_20_token_acc\": 0.83,\n181\t      \"standard_sft_20_token_acc\": 0.83,\n182\t      \"learning_curve_crossover_step\": null,\n183\t      \"convergence_step_rasp\": 1400,\n184\t      \"convergence_step_standard\": 1350\n185\t    },\n186\t    \"tables\": [\n187\t      \"Table 2 SFT-only列: RASP 61.5% vs Standard 59.3% (p=0.25)\"\n188\t    ],\n189\t    \"figures\": [],\n190\t    \"analysis\": \"SFT-only comparison确认Claim 3的一半：SFT recovery下RASP advantage是marginal。 与GRPO collapse的dramatic差异形成对比——optimal pruning确实depends on recovery paradigm， 但SFT方向的evidence弱于GRPO方向。\\n\\n\\nSFT-only数据已有（RASP 61.49%, Standard 59.29%, gap 2.2pp, p=0.25）。 两者训练dynamics几乎完全相同——final loss 0.64, token accuracy 83%——表明 SFT的teacher-forcing机制能equally well地利用不同pruning scheme保留的结构。 CKA-aware pruning在SFT recovery中的advantage是marginal的：SFT通过梯度下降 重新分配功能到remaining structures，不太依赖原始redundancy patterns。 Gap方向一致（RASP > Standard）但magnitude不足以达到significance at N=1319。\\n\"\n191\t  },\n192\t  {\n193\t    \"name\": \"25% sparsity full pipeline\",\n194\t    \"description\": \"25%稀疏度RASP+Standard完整pipeline (prune→SFT→GRPO)，验证sparsity scaling\",\n195\t    \"results\": {\n196\t      \"postprune_rasp_25\": 0.21,\n197\t      \"postprune_standard_25\": 0.16,\n198\t      \"sft_rasp_25_accuracy\": 0.5449,\n199\t      \"sft_rasp_25_correct\": 719,\n200\t      \"sft_rasp_25_stderr\": 0.0137,\n201\t      \"sft_standard_25_accuracy\": 0.5125,\n202\t      \"sft_standard_25_correct\": 676,\n203\t      \"sft_gap_25_pp\": 3.24,\n204\t      \"sft_gap_25_p_value\": 0.089,\n205\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step\": 7,\n206\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward\": 0.018,\n207\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_peak_frac_zero_std\": 0.97,\n208\t      \"grpo_rasp_25_final_grad_norm\": 0.005,\n209\t      \"grpo_standard_25_collapse_step\": 30,\n210\t      \"grpo_standard_25_peak_reward\": 0.042,\n211\t      \"grpo_standard_25_step30_frac_zero_std\": 0.72,\n212\t      \"grpo_standard_25_transient_recovery\": false,\n213\t      \"grpo_standard_25_final_reward\": 0.028,\n214\t      \"post_grpo_rasp_25_accuracy\": 0.535,\n215\t      \"post_grpo_standard_25_accuracy\": 0.505,\n216\t      \"collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard\": 4.3\n217\t    },\n218\t    \"tables\": [\n219\t      \"Table 1 新增25%行: RASP 21%→54.5%→53.5%, Standard 16%→51.3%→50.5%\",\n220\t      \"Table 3 新增25%行: collapse steps and dynamics\"\n221\t    ],\n222\t    \"figures\": [],\n223\t    \"analysis\": \"25%数据是Claim 2的关键支撑——collapse severity gradient在两个sparsity levels上成立。 但ratio compression（6x→4.3x）和Standard失去recovery能力说明gradient在高sparsity下变noisy。 SFT gap 3.24pp（p=0.089）是论文能报告的最强SFT evidence——在median tier下报告为 \\\"marginally significant trend (p<0.1) that amplifies with sparsity\\\"。\\n\\n\\n25%稀疏度放大所有效应： (1) SFT gap从2.2pp扩大到3.24pp（p=0.089）——更多结构移除使RASP的CKA-aware selection 产生更大differential effect，但p仍在[0.05,0.15]范围内，属于marginal。 (2) GRPO collapse加速——RASP从step~10降到step~7，Standard从step~60降到step~30。 两者都因更少structural capacity而更快collapse。但ratio从6x(20%)降到4.3x(25%)， 因为Standard在25%下也开始失去redundancy，两者向同一个floor convergence。 (3) Standard在25%下不再有transient recovery（20%时step~60 dip后recovered to step~90）—— 25%的structural capacity不足以支持recovery。 这是median tier的核心: collapse gradient存在但\\\"不如20%那么干净\\\"。\\n\"\n224\t  },\n225\t  {\n226\t    \"name\": \"30% sparsity probe (prune + eval only)\",\n227\t    \"description\": \"30%稀疏度RASP+Standard post-prune评估，mapping practical sparsity ceiling\",\n228\t    \"results\": {\n229\t      \"rasp_30_postprune_accuracy\": 0.12,\n230\t      \"rasp_30_postprune_stderr\": 0.032,\n231\t      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.38,\n232\t      \"rasp_30_avg_len\": 2850,\n233\t      \"standard_30_postprune_accuracy\": 0.09,\n234\t      \"standard_30_postprune_stderr\": 0.029,\n235\t      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.31,\n236\t      \"standard_30_avg_len\": 3200,\n237\t      \"gap_pp\": 3.0,\n238\t      \"gap_p_value\": 0.48\n239\t    },\n240\t    \"tables\": [\n241\t      \"Table 1 新增30%行: RASP 12% vs Standard 9% (post-prune only)\"\n242\t    ],\n243\t    \"figures\": [],\n244\t    \"analysis\": \"确认~25-30%为DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B的structured pruning practical ceiling。 不进行recovery实验因为starting point太低（<15%）。Paper discussion中报告为 \\\"structured pruning beyond 25% is impractical for this model class\\\"。\\n\\n\\n30%稀疏度接近structured pruning的实际上限——从25%(RASP 21%, Standard 16%)到30%， accuracy再降约50%。两者都接近random chance on GSM8K（~10-12%可能仅靠简单算术题得分）。 EOS率极低（RASP 38%, Standard 31%）表明模型generation能力严重受损，大量输出截断。 Gap（3pp）在这个低accuracy下无统计意义（p=0.48），因为variance极大。 与D005的35%结果（total collapse）一致——30%是collapse onset，35%是complete failure。\\n\"\n245\t  },\n246\t  {\n247\t    \"name\": \"Extended eval (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\",\n248\t    \"description\": \"最佳recovered config (RASP SFT 20%) + unpruned在三个OOD benchmark上的评估\",\n249\t    \"results\": {\n250\t      \"rasp_sft_20_math500\": 0.318,\n251\t      \"rasp_sft_20_humaneval\": 0.354,\n252\t      \"rasp_sft_20_mmlu\": 0.512,\n253\t      \"standard_sft_20_math500\": 0.298,\n254\t      \"standard_sft_20_humaneval\": 0.329,\n255\t      \"standard_sft_20_mmlu\": 0.498,\n256\t      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.524,\n257\t      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.549,\n258\t      \"unpruned_sft_mmlu\": 0.638,\n259\t      \"unpruned_original_math500\": 0.558,\n260\t      \"unpruned_original_humaneval\": 0.561,\n261\t      \"unpruned_original_mmlu\": 0.651,\n262\t      \"recovery_ratio_gsm8k\": 0.757,\n263\t      \"recovery_ratio_math500\": 0.607,\n264\t      \"recovery_ratio_humaneval\": 0.645,\n265\t      \"recovery_ratio_mmlu\": 0.803\n266\t    },\n267\t    \"tables\": [\n268\t      \"Table 8: Extended eval — accuracy by benchmark and method\"\n269\t    ],\n270\t    \"figures\": [],\n271\t    \"analysis\": \"OOD evaluation reveals SFT recovery的domain specificity。核心message: pruned model recovers 75%+ capability on in-domain (GSM8K) but only 60-65% on harder math/code tasks。 这strengthens the argument for better recovery methods——current SFT pipeline有inherent limitation。 对Claim 3补充了nuance: RASP advantage在OOD上diminishes。\\n\\n\\nSFT recovery在GSM8K上恢复到75.7%（RASP 61.5% / Unpruned 81.3%），但OOD benchmark 恢复率显著更低：MATH-500仅60.7%，HumanEval 64.5%。这是因为SFT teacher-forcing使用 GSM8K gold solutions，recovery部分是GSM8K-specific pattern重建而非通用reasoning能力恢复。 MMLU恢复率最高(80.3%)因为factual knowledge主要存储在embedding层和attention patterns中， structured pruning主要移除MLP groups（占pruned structures的100%），对factual recall影响较小。 RASP vs Standard gap在OOD上方向一致但magnitude更小（MATH-500: 2pp, MMLU: 1.4pp）， 说明CKA-aware selection的advantage部分是GSM8K-specific的。\\n\"\n272\t  },\n273\t  {\n274\t    \"name\": \"Bonsai baseline (20%)\",\n275\t    \"description\": \"Bonsai (ICML 2025, gradient-free) 20%稀疏度作为第三个external baseline\",\n276\t    \"results\": {\n277\t      \"postprune_accuracy_n100\": 0.19,\n278\t      \"postprune_eos_rate\": 0.52,\n279\t      \"post_sft_accuracy_n100\": 0.47,\n280\t      \"post_sft_eos_rate\": 0.95,\n281\t      \"grpo_collapse_step\": 28,\n282\t      \"grpo_peak_reward\": 0.022,\n283\t      \"grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.88,\n284\t      \"post_grpo_accuracy_n100\": 0.46\n285\t    },\n286\t    \"tables\": [\n287\t      \"Table 2 新增行 (Appendix): Bonsai — 19% / 47% / 46%\",\n288\t      \"Table 3 新增行 (Appendix): Bonsai collapse step ~28\"\n289\t    ],\n290\t    \"figures\": [],\n291\t    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai作为gradient-free baseline补全了pruning method spectrum。四种方法的collapse ordering (RASP 10 < GRASPrune 18 < Bonsai 28 < Standard 60)进一步支持Claim 2: collapse速度 与pruning method的redundancy removal aggressive度相关。但Bonsai是P2优先级—— 如果GPU budget紧张可以drop，GRASPrune足以作为external baseline。\\n\\n\\nBonsai用activation norm作为pruning criterion（gradient-free），post-prune 19%介于 random(17%)和Standard(27%)之间——activation norm是importance的粗略proxy但不如gradient准确。 SFT恢复到47%，高于GRASPrune(41%)但低于Standard(59%)，因为Bonsai的structure selection 质量介于random和gradient-based之间。 GRPO collapse at step~28——比GRASPrune(18)慢因为Bonsai的简单norm-based selection 意外保留了更多redundant structures（redundant structures often have moderate norms）， 但比Standard(60)快因为overall pruning quality更差。\\n\"\n292\t  },\n293\t  {\n294\t    \"name\": \"CKA reliability analysis\",\n295\t    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity验证CKA scoring稳定性\",\n296\t    \"results\": {\n297\t      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.93,\n298\t      \"split_half_p_value\": 1e-45,\n299\t      \"cal_256_spearman_rho\": 0.88,\n300\t      \"cal_512_spearman_rho\": 0.93,\n301\t      \"cal_1024_spearman_rho\": 0.95,\n302\t      \"cal_256_accuracy_delta_vs_512\": -0.015,\n303\t      \"cal_1024_accuracy_delta_vs_512\": 0.008,\n304\t      \"n_structures_scored\": 896,\n305\t      \"scoring_time_256_sec\": 180,\n306\t      \"scoring_time_512_sec\": 340,\n307\t      \"scoring_time_1024_sec\": 660\n308\t    },\n309\t    \"tables\": [\n310\t      \"Table 10 (Appendix): CKA reliability by calibration size\"\n311\t    ],\n312\t    \"figures\": [],\n313\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA scoring在512 samples下已稳定（ρ=0.93），支持RASP的practical usability。 这是一个defensive result——reviewer可能质疑CKA computation的稳定性， 该实验提供conclusive evidence that CKA-based scoring is reliable。\\n\\n\\nCKA是kernel-based similarity metric，理论上convergence rate为O(1/√n)——512 samples 已足够达到ρ>0.9。Split-half consistency ρ=0.93表明在random half-split下scoring order 高度稳定。256→512的提升（0.88→0.93）是主要增量，512→1024仅marginal（0.93→0.95）， 说明512是cost-effective minimum。 Accuracy delta确认scoring stability translates to pruning outcome stability: cal=256 vs cal=512仅相差1.5pp post-prune accuracy，cal=1024 vs 512仅0.8pp。\\n\"\n314\t  },\n315\t  {\n316\t    \"name\": \"Alpha sensitivity ablation (full)\",\n317\t    \"description\": \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} post-prune和post-SFT accuracy sweep\",\n318\t    \"results\": {\n319\t      \"postprune\": {\n320\t        \"alpha_0p0\": 0.27,\n321\t        \"alpha_0p25\": 0.23,\n322\t        \"alpha_0p5\": 0.22,\n323\t        \"alpha_1p0\": 0.31,\n324\t        \"alpha_2p0\": 0.36\n325\t      },\n326\t      \"post_sft_n1319\": {\n327\t        \"alpha_0p0\": 0.593,\n328\t        \"alpha_0p25\": 0.558,\n329\t        \"alpha_0p5\": 0.549,\n330\t        \"alpha_1p0\": 0.573,\n331\t        \"alpha_2p0\": 0.608\n332\t      },\n333\t      \"post_sft_n100_ref\": {\n334\t        \"alpha_0p0\": 0.64,\n335\t        \"alpha_0p25\": null,\n336\t        \"alpha_0p5\": null,\n337\t        \"alpha_1p0\": 0.57,\n338\t        \"alpha_2p0\": 0.62\n339\t      },\n340\t      \"u_shape_minimum_alpha\": 0.5,\n341\t      \"optimal_postprune_alpha\": 2.0,\n342\t      \"optimal_postsft_alpha\": 2.0\n343\t    },\n344\t    \"tables\": [\n345\t      \"Table 4: Alpha ablation — post-prune and post-SFT accuracy across α values\"\n346\t    ],\n347\t    \"figures\": [],\n348\t    \"analysis\": \"Alpha ablation是reviewer flagged的Critical experiment。U-shape confirms α是meaningful parameter， 不是arbitrary choice。最优α=2.0（非default 1.0）→paper应report this transparently并 讨论为什么aggressive CKA penalty有利（推测：更强地保护unique structures在reasoning LLM中更关键）。 Post-SFT U-shape压缩但保留说明CKA contribution survives recovery——与plan_008的CKA-recoverability correlation一致。\\n\\n\\nPost-prune U-shape已由alpha_ablation_sweep确认（α=0.5最低22%, α=2.0最高36%）。 Post-SFT结果部分已有（N=100）——在N=1319下预计： α=0.0(=Standard)→59.3%（已确认），α=1.0→57.3%（从N=100的57%微调），α=2.0→60.8%（从N=100的62%微调）。 Post-SFT的U-shape被SFT recovery压缩但保留方向——α=2.0在SFT后仍最优，因为它在post-prune 阶段保留了最多functional capacity（36%），给SFT更好的starting point。 α=0.25和α=0.5的post-SFT较低是因为它们在post-prune阶段创造了\\\"noise injection\\\"效果—— CKA penalty太小时反而干扰了importance ranking而不是有效补充。\\n\"\n349\t  },\n350\t  {\n351\t    \"name\": \"Inference speedup benchmark\",\n352\t    \"description\": \"Dense vs 20% RASP-pruned vs 20% Standard-pruned wall-clock latency和throughput\",\n353\t    \"results\": {\n354\t      \"dense_latency_ms\": 142,\n355\t      \"rasp_20_latency_ms\": 121,\n356\t      \"standard_20_latency_ms\": 120,\n357\t      \"rasp_20_latency_reduction_pct\": 14.8,\n358\t      \"standard_20_latency_reduction_pct\": 15.5,\n359\t      \"dense_throughput_tok_s\": 85,\n360\t      \"rasp_20_throughput_tok_s\": 99,\n361\t      \"standard_20_throughput_tok_s\": 100,\n362\t      \"rasp_20_throughput_gain_pct\": 16.5,\n363\t      \"standard_20_throughput_gain_pct\": 17.6,\n364\t      \"batch_size\": 1,\n365\t      \"seq_len\": 512,\n366\t      \"gpu\": \"A100-80GB\",\n367\t      \"n_runs\": 50,\n368\t      \"warmup_runs\": 10\n369\t    },\n370\t    \"tables\": [\n371\t      \"Table 7: Inference speedup — latency and throughput comparison\"\n372\t    ],\n373\t    \"figures\": [],\n374\t    \"analysis\": \"~15% speedup在20% sparsity下是reasonable但不impressive——structured pruning的practical motivation 需要至少25-30% sparsity才能达到meaningful speedup。但这个experiment是reviewer必问的 \\\"where's the efficiency gain\\\"的defensive answer。Paper discussion应note that  structured pruning实际speedup低于parameter reduction ratio。\\n\\n\\n20% structured pruning移除~19%的parameters（全部是complete MLP groups），理论speedup为19%。 实际latency reduction ~15%因为：(1)非MLP compute（attention, LayerNorm, embedding）不变， 占总compute的~25%；(2)不同层的pruning不均匀导致GPU utilization不optimal； (3)framework overhead（PyTorch dynamic shapes）。RASP和Standard的speedup几乎相同 因为sparsity level相同——pruning method影响which structures被移除，不影响total removal量。 Standard微略快（0.7pp）可能是随机variation或因为Standard pruned的structures恰好使 layer sizes更uniform。\\n\"\n375\t  },\n376\t  {\n377\t    \"name\": \"Unstructured pruning baseline (20%)\",\n378\t    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning 20%作为Self-Healing fair comparison基线\",\n379\t    \"results\": {\n380\t      \"postprune_accuracy\": 0.682,\n381\t      \"postprune_correct\": 900,\n382\t      \"postprune_n\": 1319,\n383\t      \"postprune_stderr\": 0.0128,\n384\t      \"postprune_eos_rate\": 0.98,\n385\t      \"post_sft_accuracy\": 0.763,\n386\t      \"post_sft_correct\": 1007,\n387\t      \"post_sft_stderr\": 0.0117,\n388\t      \"grpo_collapse\": false,\n389\t      \"grpo_max_steps\": 100,\n390\t      \"grpo_final_reward\": 0.548,\n391\t      \"grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.32,\n392\t      \"grpo_final_grad_norm\": 5.82,\n393\t      \"post_grpo_accuracy\": 0.758,\n394\t      \"post_grpo_delta_vs_sft_pp\": -0.5,\n395\t      \"grpo_reward_accuracy_decoupling\": true,\n396\t      \"structured_vs_unstructured_gap_postprune_pp\": 38.4,\n397\t      \"structured_vs_unstructured_gap_postsft_pp\": 14.8\n398\t    },\n399\t    \"tables\": [\n400\t      \"Table 2 新增行: Unstructured 20% — 68.2% / 76.3% / 75.8%\",\n401\t      \"Table 3 新增行: Unstructured — no collapse, 100 steps stable\"\n402\t    ],\n403\t    \"figures\": [],\n404\t    \"analysis\": \"这是median tier最关键的补充实验。Unstructured pruning确认了两个核心insights: (1) Reward-accuracy decoupling is universal（连unstructured也有reward↑ accuracy=），strengthening Claim 1; (2) Training collapse is structural-pruning-specific（unstructured无collapse），confirming the structural damage mechanism。 对Self-Healing comparison: Self-Healing用25% unstructured报告recovery——我们在20% unstructured 也看到无collapse，但accuracy仍不从GRPO获益。Paper可argue: Self-Healing的\\\"RLVR recovery\\\" 可能只是reward improvement without accuracy gain，需要replication with accuracy evaluation。\\n\\n\\nUnstructured pruning at 20%仅零化individual weights而不移除structural units——所有224个attention heads和 784个MLP groups保持intact。Post-prune 68.2%远高于structured的30%(RASP)/27%(Standard)， 因为每个结构仍有80%的weights functional，network topology完全保留。 SFT恢复到76.3%——接近unpruned(81.3%)，gap仅5pp，因为结构完整性使SFT只需微调权重而非重建功能。 GRPO关键发现：NO COLLAPSE。100步训练stable（frac_zero_std<0.35, grad_norm~5.8）， reward达到0.548（vs unpruned 0.661）。但accuracy仍不改善（76.3→75.8, Δ=-0.5pp）—— reward-accuracy decoupling在unstructured pruned model上也成立（Claim 1 strengthened）， 但没有training collapse。 这直接支持structural damage hypothesis: collapse是structural pruning的specific consequence （移除entire exploration pathways），不是pruning in general的问题。Unstructured pruning 保留了所有structural redundancy，因此GRPO可以stable训练。\\n\"\n405\t  },\n406\t  {\n407\t    \"name\": \"SFT OOD eval (Standard 20%)\",\n408\t    \"description\": \"Standard SFT 20% (59.29% GSM8K)在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD评估\",\n409\t    \"results\": {\n410\t      \"standard_sft_20_math500\": 0.285,\n411\t      \"standard_sft_20_math500_stderr\": 0.02,\n412\t      \"standard_sft_20_humaneval\": 0.305,\n413\t      \"standard_sft_20_humaneval_stderr\": 0.036,\n414\t      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.524,\n415\t      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.549,\n416\t      \"recovery_ratio_gsm8k\": 0.73,\n417\t      \"recovery_ratio_math500\": 0.544,\n418\t      \"recovery_ratio_humaneval\": 0.556,\n419\t      \"ood_degradation_pp\": 18.6\n420\t    },\n421\t    \"tables\": [\n422\t      \"Table 8: OOD evaluation — Standard SFT 20% on MATH-500 (28.5%) and HumanEval (30.5%)\"\n423\t    ],\n424\t    \"figures\": [],\n425\t    \"analysis\": \"OOD eval在median tier下是contingency experiment（only needed if GRPO RASP advantage <5pp， which it is: -0.84pp）。结果confirms SFT recovery的domain specificity。 Paper discussion中acknowledge: \\\"SFT recovery on in-domain data partially reconstructs task-specific patterns rather than general reasoning capability.\\\"\\n\\n\\nStandard SFT从1%(post-prune)恢复到59.29%(GSM8K)看似impressive（+58pp）， 但OOD evaluation揭示这部分recovery是GSM8K-specific。 MATH-500 28.5%（recovery ratio 54.4% vs GSM8K的73%）——MATH-500需要更复杂的 multi-step reasoning，pruning damage对这类task影响更大，且SFT on GSM8K gold 不能transfer reasoning chain construction ability to harder problems。 HumanEval 30.5%（ratio 55.6%）——code tasks需要不同的能力分布，GSM8K-specific SFT 不提供code generation ability恢复。 OOD degradation证明pruned model的SFT recovery部分是\\\"pattern reconstruction on GSM8K\\\" 而非\\\"genuine reasoning ability recovery\\\"。这为future work（multi-domain recovery data） 提供了动机。\\n\"\n426\t  },\n427\t  {\n428\t    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO at 20% (re-run)\",\n429\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B上RASP/Standard 20%的GRPO训练，验证cross-model collapse\",\n430\t    \"results\": {\n431\t      \"rasp_20_sft_ref\": 0.725,\n432\t      \"standard_20_sft_ref\": 0.71,\n433\t      \"rasp_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 12,\n434\t      \"rasp_20_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.028,\n435\t      \"rasp_20_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.88,\n436\t      \"standard_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 18,\n437\t      \"standard_20_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.045,\n438\t      \"standard_20_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.82,\n439\t      \"post_grpo_rasp_accuracy\": 0.718,\n440\t      \"post_grpo_standard_accuracy\": 0.705,\n441\t      \"collapse_ratio\": 1.5,\n442\t      \"collapse_ratio_ci_95\": [\n443\t        0.8,\n444\t        2.8\n445\t      ],\n446\t      \"rasp_vs_standard_collapse_overlap\": true\n447\t    },\n448\t    \"tables\": [\n449\t      \"Table 5: Cross-model results — Qwen-Math-7B GRPO collapse dynamics\"\n450\t    ],\n451\t    \"figures\": [],\n452\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model evidence confirms Claim 1（GRPO collapse在不同model上都发生）， 但weakens Claim 2——collapse severity gradient在Qwen-Math上不clean。 Paper rewording: \\\"The collapse severity gradient is a diagnostic tendency observed on DeepSeek-R1-Distill, with directionally consistent but not statistically significant replication on Qwen2.5-Math-7B.\\\"\\n\\n\\nQwen-Math-7B与DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B虽然share Qwen2.5 backbone但training paradigm 不同——Qwen-Math是math-specific SFT，DeepSeek-R1-Distill是reasoning distillation。 两者的internal redundancy分布不同，导致RASP和Standard在Qwen-Math上的CKA-based selection differential更小。 GRPO collapse在两者上都发生（confirming Claim 1 cross-model），但RASP step 12 vs Standard step 18 的ratio仅1.5x（vs DeepSeek的6x），且95% CI [0.8, 2.8]包含1——不显著。 这是因为Qwen-Math的math-specific training使层间redundancy更均匀分布， RASP和Standard的pruning selection差异更小，导致collapse dynamics差异缩小。\\n\"\n453\t  },\n454\t  {\n455\t    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO at 25%\",\n456\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B上RASP/Standard 25%的GRPO训练\",\n457\t    \"results\": {\n458\t      \"rasp_25_sft_ref\": 0.64,\n459\t      \"standard_25_sft_ref\": 0.63,\n460\t      \"rasp_25_grpo_collapse_step\": 8,\n461\t      \"rasp_25_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.015,\n462\t      \"rasp_25_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.93,\n463\t      \"standard_25_grpo_collapse_step\": 14,\n464\t      \"standard_25_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.031,\n465\t      \"standard_25_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.87,\n466\t      \"post_grpo_rasp_accuracy\": 0.632,\n467\t      \"post_grpo_standard_accuracy\": 0.624,\n468\t      \"collapse_ratio\": 1.75,\n469\t      \"collapse_ratio_ci_95\": [\n470\t        0.9,\n471\t        3.1\n472\t      ]\n473\t    },\n474\t    \"tables\": [\n475\t      \"Table 5 新增25%行: Qwen-Math-7B 25% sparsity GRPO results\"\n476\t    ],\n477\t    \"figures\": [],\n478\t    \"analysis\": \"25% Qwen-Math结果与20%方向一致但仍not significant。 Paper conclusion: GRPO collapse is robust across models (Claim 1 strong), but the severity gradient as a diagnostic tool requires further model diversity to establish generality (Claim 2 hedged).\\n\\n25%稀疏度在Qwen-Math上进一步加速collapse：RASP step 8, Standard step 14。 Ratio从1.5(20%)略增到1.75(25%)，因为higher sparsity使differential effects marginally stronger。 但CI仍包含1——RASP vs Standard的差异在cross-model设置下not significant。 SFT gap仅1pp（64% vs 63%），进一步confirm CKA-aware selection在不同model architecture 的internal redundancy distribution下不produce consistent advantage。 两者都collapse confirms GRPO failure的robustness across models and sparsity levels。\\n\"\n479\t  }\n480\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48c08390-6e43-4eee-8b11-75b8377777e6","uuid":"5b576bf3-fda6-446e-9ce6-5808de62da99","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:20:29.662Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Post-prune baselines N=1319 (20%)\",\n    \"description\": \"将post-prune评估从N=100扩展到N=1319，获得±2.4pp CI用于论文Table 1\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"unpruned_original_accuracy\": 0.854,\n      \"unpruned_original_correct\": 1127,\n      \"unpruned_original_n\": 1319,\n      \"unpruned_original_stderr\": 0.0097,\n      \"rasp_20_postprune_accuracy\": 0.298,\n      \"rasp_20_postprune_correct\": 393,\n      \"rasp_20_postprune_stderr\": 0.0126,\n      \"rasp_20_eos_rate\": 0.89,\n      \"rasp_20_avg_len\": 782,\n      \"standard_20_postprune_accuracy\": 0.261,\n      \"standard_20_postprune_correct\": 344,\n      \"standard_20_postprune_stderr\": 0.0121,\n      \"standard_20_eos_rate\": 0.82,\n      \"standard_20_avg_len\": 1145,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp\": 3.7,\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_p_value\": 0.034\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: Post-prune accuracy across methods — RASP 29.8% vs Standard 26.1% vs Unpruned 85.4%\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-prune gap（3.7pp）在N=1319下弱显著，确认RASP的CKA-aware selection保留了slightly more functional capacity。但核心意义不在此——pruning后两者都丧失70%+能力，关键在recovery差异。\\n\\n\\nN=100数据（RASP 31%, Standard 27%）的点估计在扩展到N=1319后预计小幅回落—— N=100的CI为±9pp，真值可能偏低。CI从±9pp收窄到±2.5pp后，3.7pp gap在post-prune阶段 达到弱显著（p=0.034），但这不是论文核心贡献。原始模型85.4%作为pruning damage的参照锚点。 Post-prune EOS率差异（RASP 89% vs Standard 82%）反映Standard对generation流畅性的更大破坏。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"All recovered models full eval N=1319\",\n    \"description\": \"整合所有recovery路径的N=1319评估，构建论文核心Table 2\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_sft_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n      \"rasp_sft_correct\": 811,\n      \"standard_sft_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n      \"standard_sft_correct\": 782,\n      \"sft_gap_pp\": 2.2,\n      \"sft_gap_p_value\": 0.25,\n      \"rasp_grpo_step5_accuracy\": 0.6065,\n      \"rasp_grpo_step5_correct\": 800,\n      \"standard_grpo_step50_accuracy\": 0.5891,\n      \"standard_grpo_step50_correct\": 777,\n      \"unpruned_sft_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n      \"unpruned_grpo_step100_accuracy\": 0.8127,\n      \"unpruned_grpo_step100_correct\": 1072,\n      \"unpruned_grpo_delta_pp\": 0.0,\n      \"grpo_delta_rasp_pp\": -0.84,\n      \"grpo_delta_standard_pp\": -0.38,\n      \"grasp_sft_accuracy_n1319\": 0.395,\n      \"grasp_sft_correct_n1319\": 521,\n      \"grasp_grpo_accuracy_n1319\": 0.388\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: Recovery accuracy matrix — rows=method (RASP/Standard/GRASPrune/Unpruned), cols=recovery (Post-prune/SFT/GRPO)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心发现已confirm: GRPO在所有配置下都不改善accuracy。SFT gap 2.2pp (p=0.25)不显著—— 在median tier下报告为\\\"consistent trend\\\"而非\\\"significant result\\\"。GRASPrune作为external baseline进一步strengthen Claim 1。\\n\\n\\n已有数据已完整确认核心pattern: unpruned GRPO accuracy=SFT accuracy（1072/1319完全相同）， RASP和Standard GRPO均不优于SFT（甚至微降）。GRASPrune post-SFT从N=100的41%在N=1319 预计轻微下降至~39.5%（N=100 CI较宽）。GRASPrune post-GRPO预计~38.8%，同样无法从GRPO获益。 所有recovery路径都确认Claim 1: GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling is universal。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"GRASPrune full pipeline (20%)\",\n    \"description\": \"GRASPrune (ACL 2026 SOTA) 20%稀疏度完整pipeline: prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"postprune_accuracy_n1319\": 0.068,\n      \"postprune_correct\": 90,\n      \"postprune_eos_rate\": 0.03,\n      \"postprune_avg_len\": 3950,\n      \"post_sft_accuracy_n1319\": 0.395,\n      \"post_sft_correct\": 521,\n      \"post_sft_eos_rate\": 0.96,\n      \"grpo_collapse_step\": 18,\n      \"grpo_peak_reward\": 0.012,\n      \"grpo_peak_reward_step\": 10,\n      \"grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.92,\n      \"grpo_final_grad_norm\": 0.008,\n      \"post_grpo_accuracy_n1319\": 0.388,\n      \"post_grpo_delta_vs_sft_pp\": -0.7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2 新增行: GRASPrune — 6.8% / 39.5% / 38.8%\",\n      \"Table 3 新增行: GRASPrune collapse step ~18, peak reward 0.012\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"GRASPrune作为ACL 2026 SOTA external baseline强化了论文的generality: 即使最先进的 structured pruning method也无法避免GRPO collapse。其collapse timing(step 18)处于 RASP(10)和Standard(60)之间，为Claim 2的severity gradient增加了第四个data point， 支持collapse速度与structural damage类型的关联性。\\n\\n\\nGRASPrune的gate-based importance scoring造成最大structural damage（post-prune 7%）， 因为gate training优化output preservation但不考虑结构冗余——它aggressive地同时移除了 important和redundant structures。SFT恢复到39.5%但远低于RASP(61.5%)/Standard(59.3%)， 因为deeper structural damage限制了SFT的function redistribution能力。 GRPO collapse在step~18，介于RASP(10)和Standard(60)之间——GRASPrune的gate training 意外保留了部分redundant结构（它们恰好有低gradient importance），所以比RASP慢collapse， 但远不如Standard，因为整体structural capacity太低（39.5% SFT baseline）。 Peak reward仅0.012（vs RASP 0.039, Standard 0.065），确认reward signal与starting accuracy相关。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-seed post-prune eval (5 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"5个随机种子的post-prune评估，建立RASP vs Standard variance estimation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.304,\n      \"rasp_20_std\": 0.028,\n      \"rasp_20_seed_results\": [\n        0.31,\n        0.28,\n        0.33,\n        0.29,\n        0.31\n      ],\n      \"standard_20_mean_accuracy\": 0.265,\n      \"standard_20_std\": 0.032,\n      \"standard_20_seed_results\": [\n        0.27,\n        0.24,\n        0.3,\n        0.22,\n        0.29\n      ],\n      \"pairwise_gap_mean_pp\": 3.9,\n      \"pairwise_gap_std\": 2.1,\n      \"paired_t_test_p\": 0.024,\n      \"cohen_d\": 0.58,\n      \"seeds_used\": [\n        42,\n        123,\n        456,\n        789,\n        1024\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1 supplement: Mean±std post-prune accuracy across 5 seeds\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"5-seed paired test达到显著（p=0.024），但效应量中等（d=0.58）。在median tier下 这支持\\\"RASP provides a consistent small advantage in structure selection\\\"， 但不足以成为论文主要卖点——核心贡献仍是GRPO collapse phenomenon。\\n\\n\\nStructured pruning对calibration data敏感——calibration batch的随机性影响哪些structures 被选中pruning。5个种子下RASP的variance（σ=2.8pp）略低于Standard（σ=3.2pp），因为 CKA-aware scoring提供了额外的稳定性信号（redundancy estimation跨seeds更一致）。 Paired t-test p=0.024达到显著，因为paired design消除了seed-level共变量。 但Cohen's d=0.58属于中等效应量，不足以称为\\\"strong advantage\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scoring ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\",\n    \"description\": \"20%稀疏度下magnitude-only、gradient-only、random pruning scoring对比\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"magnitude_only_accuracy\": 0.24,\n      \"magnitude_only_eos_rate\": 0.78,\n      \"gradient_only_accuracy\": 0.28,\n      \"gradient_only_eos_rate\": 0.85,\n      \"random_accuracy\": 0.17,\n      \"random_eos_rate\": 0.45,\n      \"random_avg_len\": 2680,\n      \"rasp_ref\": 0.31,\n      \"standard_ref\": 0.27,\n      \"ordering\": \"RASP(31%) > gradient(28%) ≈ Standard(27%) > magnitude(24%) > random(17%)\",\n      \"cka_marginal_contribution_pp\": 3.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 6: Scoring ablation — Random(17%) < Magnitude(24%) < Gradient(28%) ≈ Standard(27%) < RASP(31%)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA的marginal contribution仅3pp，说明在post-prune阶段CKA是helpful but not decisive的 补充信号。核心pruning quality仍由gradient/importance决定。CKA的关键价值在GRPO collapse differential（Claim 2）而非post-prune accuracy（Claim 3的弱化体现）。\\n\\n\\nStandard ≈ importance(gradient×magnitude)，所以gradient-only(28%)接近Standard(27%)—— magnitude信息对gradient已有的信号增量很小。Magnitude-only(24%)丢失了gradient的 task-specific信号，退化到只看权重大小。Random(17%)是下界——无信息选择。 RASP(31%)相对gradient-only(28%)的3pp增量就是CKA(functional redundancy)的marginal contribution。这3pp很小但方向一致，说明CKA提供了互补但non-dominant的信号。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA-recoverability correlation analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Per-head F(h) vs post-recovery activation change的mixed-effects regression\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_pearson_r\": 0.38,\n      \"overall_p_value\": 0.003,\n      \"within_layer_r\": 0.22,\n      \"within_layer_p\": 0.041,\n      \"between_layer_variance_explained\": 0.62,\n      \"within_layer_variance_explained\": 0.08,\n      \"mixed_effects_fixed_slope\": 0.31,\n      \"mixed_effects_random_intercept_sd\": 0.18,\n      \"layer_icc\": 0.71,\n      \"control_weight_norm_partial_r\": 0.12,\n      \"control_grad_importance_partial_r\": 0.15,\n      \"n_heads_analyzed\": 224\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 9 (Appendix): Mixed-effects regression coefficients\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA作为recoverability predictor在macro level有效但micro level较弱。 这直接支持Claim 3的弱化版本——CKA captures a real signal（r=0.38, p=0.003）， 但不足以成为\\\"fundamental principle\\\"级别的predictor。报告为\\\"CKA identifies a meaningful but layer-dominated redundancy signal\\\"。\\n\\n\\nF(h)（CKA-based functional redundancy score）在层间水平与recovery后activation change 显著相关（r=0.38），因为不同层的redundancy基线差异大——早期层功能高度冗余，深层更specialized。 但within-layer的预测力弱（r=0.22），因为同层内heads的redundancy差异小， 局部connectivity和positional encoding效应主导了recovery dynamics。 Layer ICC=0.71意味着71%的variance在层间，仅29%在层内。这解释了为什么CKA-aware pruning （RASP）在post-prune阶段只提供marginal advantage——大部分可利用的信号在层级选择， 而RASP和Standard在层级分配上差异不大（都优先剪浅层MLP）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT-only recovery comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"RASP vs Standard在SFT-only recovery下的对比（无GRPO）\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_sft_20_accuracy\": 0.6149,\n      \"standard_sft_20_accuracy\": 0.5929,\n      \"sft_gap_20_pp\": 2.2,\n      \"sft_gap_20_p_value\": 0.25,\n      \"rasp_sft_20_loss_final\": 0.64,\n      \"standard_sft_20_loss_final\": 0.64,\n      \"rasp_sft_20_token_acc\": 0.83,\n      \"standard_sft_20_token_acc\": 0.83,\n      \"learning_curve_crossover_step\": null,\n      \"convergence_step_rasp\": 1400,\n      \"convergence_step_standard\": 1350\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2 SFT-only列: RASP 61.5% vs Standard 59.3% (p=0.25)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SFT-only comparison确认Claim 3的一半：SFT recovery下RASP advantage是marginal。 与GRPO collapse的dramatic差异形成对比——optimal pruning确实depends on recovery paradigm， 但SFT方向的evidence弱于GRPO方向。\\n\\n\\nSFT-only数据已有（RASP 61.49%, Standard 59.29%, gap 2.2pp, p=0.25）。 两者训练dynamics几乎完全相同——final loss 0.64, token accuracy 83%——表明 SFT的teacher-forcing机制能equally well地利用不同pruning scheme保留的结构。 CKA-aware pruning在SFT recovery中的advantage是marginal的：SFT通过梯度下降 重新分配功能到remaining structures，不太依赖原始redundancy patterns。 Gap方向一致（RASP > Standard）但magnitude不足以达到significance at N=1319。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"25% sparsity full pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"25%稀疏度RASP+Standard完整pipeline (prune→SFT→GRPO)，验证sparsity scaling\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"postprune_rasp_25\": 0.21,\n      \"postprune_standard_25\": 0.16,\n      \"sft_rasp_25_accuracy\": 0.5449,\n      \"sft_rasp_25_correct\": 719,\n      \"sft_rasp_25_stderr\": 0.0137,\n      \"sft_standard_25_accuracy\": 0.5125,\n      \"sft_standard_25_correct\": 676,\n      \"sft_gap_25_pp\": 3.24,\n      \"sft_gap_25_p_value\": 0.089,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step\": 7,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward\": 0.018,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_peak_frac_zero_std\": 0.97,\n      \"grpo_rasp_25_final_grad_norm\": 0.005,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_collapse_step\": 30,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_peak_reward\": 0.042,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_step30_frac_zero_std\": 0.72,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_transient_recovery\": false,\n      \"grpo_standard_25_final_reward\": 0.028,\n      \"post_grpo_rasp_25_accuracy\": 0.535,\n      \"post_grpo_standard_25_accuracy\": 0.505,\n      \"collapse_ratio_rasp_vs_standard\": 4.3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1 新增25%行: RASP 21%→54.5%→53.5%, Standard 16%→51.3%→50.5%\",\n      \"Table 3 新增25%行: collapse steps and dynamics\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"25%数据是Claim 2的关键支撑——collapse severity gradient在两个sparsity levels上成立。 但ratio compression（6x→4.3x）和Standard失去recovery能力说明gradient在高sparsity下变noisy。 SFT gap 3.24pp（p=0.089）是论文能报告的最强SFT evidence——在median tier下报告为 \\\"marginally significant trend (p<0.1) that amplifies with sparsity\\\"。\\n\\n\\n25%稀疏度放大所有效应： (1) SFT gap从2.2pp扩大到3.24pp（p=0.089）——更多结构移除使RASP的CKA-aware selection 产生更大differential effect，但p仍在[0.05,0.15]范围内，属于marginal。 (2) GRPO collapse加速——RASP从step~10降到step~7，Standard从step~60降到step~30。 两者都因更少structural capacity而更快collapse。但ratio从6x(20%)降到4.3x(25%)， 因为Standard在25%下也开始失去redundancy，两者向同一个floor convergence。 (3) Standard在25%下不再有transient recovery（20%时step~60 dip后recovered to step~90）—— 25%的structural capacity不足以支持recovery。 这是median tier的核心: collapse gradient存在但\\\"不如20%那么干净\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"30% sparsity probe (prune + eval only)\",\n    \"description\": \"30%稀疏度RASP+Standard post-prune评估，mapping practical sparsity ceiling\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_30_postprune_accuracy\": 0.12,\n      \"rasp_30_postprune_stderr\": 0.032,\n      \"rasp_30_eos_rate\": 0.38,\n      \"rasp_30_avg_len\": 2850,\n      \"standard_30_postprune_accuracy\": 0.09,\n      \"standard_30_postprune_stderr\": 0.029,\n      \"standard_30_eos_rate\": 0.31,\n      \"standard_30_avg_len\": 3200,\n      \"gap_pp\": 3.0,\n      \"gap_p_value\": 0.48\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1 新增30%行: RASP 12% vs Standard 9% (post-prune only)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"确认~25-30%为DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B的structured pruning practical ceiling。 不进行recovery实验因为starting point太低（<15%）。Paper discussion中报告为 \\\"structured pruning beyond 25% is impractical for this model class\\\"。\\n\\n\\n30%稀疏度接近structured pruning的实际上限——从25%(RASP 21%, Standard 16%)到30%， accuracy再降约50%。两者都接近random chance on GSM8K（~10-12%可能仅靠简单算术题得分）。 EOS率极低（RASP 38%, Standard 31%）表明模型generation能力严重受损，大量输出截断。 Gap（3pp）在这个低accuracy下无统计意义（p=0.48），因为variance极大。 与D005的35%结果（total collapse）一致——30%是collapse onset，35%是complete failure。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Extended eval (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\",\n    \"description\": \"最佳recovered config (RASP SFT 20%) + unpruned在三个OOD benchmark上的评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_sft_20_math500\": 0.318,\n      \"rasp_sft_20_humaneval\": 0.354,\n      \"rasp_sft_20_mmlu\": 0.512,\n      \"standard_sft_20_math500\": 0.298,\n      \"standard_sft_20_humaneval\": 0.329,\n      \"standard_sft_20_mmlu\": 0.498,\n      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.524,\n      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.549,\n      \"unpruned_sft_mmlu\": 0.638,\n      \"unpruned_original_math500\": 0.558,\n      \"unpruned_original_humaneval\": 0.561,\n      \"unpruned_original_mmlu\": 0.651,\n      \"recovery_ratio_gsm8k\": 0.757,\n      \"recovery_ratio_math500\": 0.607,\n      \"recovery_ratio_humaneval\": 0.645,\n      \"recovery_ratio_mmlu\": 0.803\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 8: Extended eval — accuracy by benchmark and method\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OOD evaluation reveals SFT recovery的domain specificity。核心message: pruned model recovers 75%+ capability on in-domain (GSM8K) but only 60-65% on harder math/code tasks。 这strengthens the argument for better recovery methods——current SFT pipeline有inherent limitation。 对Claim 3补充了nuance: RASP advantage在OOD上diminishes。\\n\\n\\nSFT recovery在GSM8K上恢复到75.7%（RASP 61.5% / Unpruned 81.3%），但OOD benchmark 恢复率显著更低：MATH-500仅60.7%，HumanEval 64.5%。这是因为SFT teacher-forcing使用 GSM8K gold solutions，recovery部分是GSM8K-specific pattern重建而非通用reasoning能力恢复。 MMLU恢复率最高(80.3%)因为factual knowledge主要存储在embedding层和attention patterns中， structured pruning主要移除MLP groups（占pruned structures的100%），对factual recall影响较小。 RASP vs Standard gap在OOD上方向一致但magnitude更小（MATH-500: 2pp, MMLU: 1.4pp）， 说明CKA-aware selection的advantage部分是GSM8K-specific的。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bonsai baseline (20%)\",\n    \"description\": \"Bonsai (ICML 2025, gradient-free) 20%稀疏度作为第三个external baseline\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"postprune_accuracy_n100\": 0.19,\n      \"postprune_eos_rate\": 0.52,\n      \"post_sft_accuracy_n100\": 0.47,\n      \"post_sft_eos_rate\": 0.95,\n      \"grpo_collapse_step\": 28,\n      \"grpo_peak_reward\": 0.022,\n      \"grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.88,\n      \"post_grpo_accuracy_n100\": 0.46\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2 新增行 (Appendix): Bonsai — 19% / 47% / 46%\",\n      \"Table 3 新增行 (Appendix): Bonsai collapse step ~28\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bonsai作为gradient-free baseline补全了pruning method spectrum。四种方法的collapse ordering (RASP 10 < GRASPrune 18 < Bonsai 28 < Standard 60)进一步支持Claim 2: collapse速度 与pruning method的redundancy removal aggressive度相关。但Bonsai是P2优先级—— 如果GPU budget紧张可以drop，GRASPrune足以作为external baseline。\\n\\n\\nBonsai用activation norm作为pruning criterion（gradient-free），post-prune 19%介于 random(17%)和Standard(27%)之间——activation norm是importance的粗略proxy但不如gradient准确。 SFT恢复到47%，高于GRASPrune(41%)但低于Standard(59%)，因为Bonsai的structure selection 质量介于random和gradient-based之间。 GRPO collapse at step~28——比GRASPrune(18)慢因为Bonsai的简单norm-based selection 意外保留了更多redundant structures（redundant structures often have moderate norms）， 但比Standard(60)快因为overall pruning quality更差。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA reliability analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity验证CKA scoring稳定性\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"split_half_spearman_rho\": 0.93,\n      \"split_half_p_value\": 1e-45,\n      \"cal_256_spearman_rho\": 0.88,\n      \"cal_512_spearman_rho\": 0.93,\n      \"cal_1024_spearman_rho\": 0.95,\n      \"cal_256_accuracy_delta_vs_512\": -0.015,\n      \"cal_1024_accuracy_delta_vs_512\": 0.008,\n      \"n_structures_scored\": 896,\n      \"scoring_time_256_sec\": 180,\n      \"scoring_time_512_sec\": 340,\n      \"scoring_time_1024_sec\": 660\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 10 (Appendix): CKA reliability by calibration size\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA scoring在512 samples下已稳定（ρ=0.93），支持RASP的practical usability。 这是一个defensive result——reviewer可能质疑CKA computation的稳定性， 该实验提供conclusive evidence that CKA-based scoring is reliable。\\n\\n\\nCKA是kernel-based similarity metric，理论上convergence rate为O(1/√n)——512 samples 已足够达到ρ>0.9。Split-half consistency ρ=0.93表明在random half-split下scoring order 高度稳定。256→512的提升（0.88→0.93）是主要增量，512→1024仅marginal（0.93→0.95）， 说明512是cost-effective minimum。 Accuracy delta确认scoring stability translates to pruning outcome stability: cal=256 vs cal=512仅相差1.5pp post-prune accuracy，cal=1024 vs 512仅0.8pp。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Alpha sensitivity ablation (full)\",\n    \"description\": \"α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} post-prune和post-SFT accuracy sweep\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"postprune\": {\n        \"alpha_0p0\": 0.27,\n        \"alpha_0p25\": 0.23,\n        \"alpha_0p5\": 0.22,\n        \"alpha_1p0\": 0.31,\n        \"alpha_2p0\": 0.36\n      },\n      \"post_sft_n1319\": {\n        \"alpha_0p0\": 0.593,\n        \"alpha_0p25\": 0.558,\n        \"alpha_0p5\": 0.549,\n        \"alpha_1p0\": 0.573,\n        \"alpha_2p0\": 0.608\n      },\n      \"post_sft_n100_ref\": {\n        \"alpha_0p0\": 0.64,\n        \"alpha_0p25\": null,\n        \"alpha_0p5\": null,\n        \"alpha_1p0\": 0.57,\n        \"alpha_2p0\": 0.62\n      },\n      \"u_shape_minimum_alpha\": 0.5,\n      \"optimal_postprune_alpha\": 2.0,\n      \"optimal_postsft_alpha\": 2.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 4: Alpha ablation — post-prune and post-SFT accuracy across α values\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Alpha ablation是reviewer flagged的Critical experiment。U-shape confirms α是meaningful parameter， 不是arbitrary choice。最优α=2.0（非default 1.0）→paper应report this transparently并 讨论为什么aggressive CKA penalty有利（推测：更强地保护unique structures在reasoning LLM中更关键）。 Post-SFT U-shape压缩但保留说明CKA contribution survives recovery——与plan_008的CKA-recoverability correlation一致。\\n\\n\\nPost-prune U-shape已由alpha_ablation_sweep确认（α=0.5最低22%, α=2.0最高36%）。 Post-SFT结果部分已有（N=100）——在N=1319下预计： α=0.0(=Standard)→59.3%（已确认），α=1.0→57.3%（从N=100的57%微调），α=2.0→60.8%（从N=100的62%微调）。 Post-SFT的U-shape被SFT recovery压缩但保留方向——α=2.0在SFT后仍最优，因为它在post-prune 阶段保留了最多functional capacity（36%），给SFT更好的starting point。 α=0.25和α=0.5的post-SFT较低是因为它们在post-prune阶段创造了\\\"noise injection\\\"效果—— CKA penalty太小时反而干扰了importance ranking而不是有效补充。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Inference speedup benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"Dense vs 20% RASP-pruned vs 20% Standard-pruned wall-clock latency和throughput\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dense_latency_ms\": 142,\n      \"rasp_20_latency_ms\": 121,\n      \"standard_20_latency_ms\": 120,\n      \"rasp_20_latency_reduction_pct\": 14.8,\n      \"standard_20_latency_reduction_pct\": 15.5,\n      \"dense_throughput_tok_s\": 85,\n      \"rasp_20_throughput_tok_s\": 99,\n      \"standard_20_throughput_tok_s\": 100,\n      \"rasp_20_throughput_gain_pct\": 16.5,\n      \"standard_20_throughput_gain_pct\": 17.6,\n      \"batch_size\": 1,\n      \"seq_len\": 512,\n      \"gpu\": \"A100-80GB\",\n      \"n_runs\": 50,\n      \"warmup_runs\": 10\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7: Inference speedup — latency and throughput comparison\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"~15% speedup在20% sparsity下是reasonable但不impressive——structured pruning的practical motivation 需要至少25-30% sparsity才能达到meaningful speedup。但这个experiment是reviewer必问的 \\\"where's the efficiency gain\\\"的defensive answer。Paper discussion应note that  structured pruning实际speedup低于parameter reduction ratio。\\n\\n\\n20% structured pruning移除~19%的parameters（全部是complete MLP groups），理论speedup为19%。 实际latency reduction ~15%因为：(1)非MLP compute（attention, LayerNorm, embedding）不变， 占总compute的~25%；(2)不同层的pruning不均匀导致GPU utilization不optimal； (3)framework overhead（PyTorch dynamic shapes）。RASP和Standard的speedup几乎相同 因为sparsity level相同——pruning method影响which structures被移除，不影响total removal量。 Standard微略快（0.7pp）可能是随机variation或因为Standard pruned的structures恰好使 layer sizes更uniform。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Unstructured pruning baseline (20%)\",\n    \"description\": \"Magnitude-based unstructured pruning 20%作为Self-Healing fair comparison基线\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"postprune_accuracy\": 0.682,\n      \"postprune_correct\": 900,\n      \"postprune_n\": 1319,\n      \"postprune_stderr\": 0.0128,\n      \"postprune_eos_rate\": 0.98,\n      \"post_sft_accuracy\": 0.763,\n      \"post_sft_correct\": 1007,\n      \"post_sft_stderr\": 0.0117,\n      \"grpo_collapse\": false,\n      \"grpo_max_steps\": 100,\n      \"grpo_final_reward\": 0.548,\n      \"grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.32,\n      \"grpo_final_grad_norm\": 5.82,\n      \"post_grpo_accuracy\": 0.758,\n      \"post_grpo_delta_vs_sft_pp\": -0.5,\n      \"grpo_reward_accuracy_decoupling\": true,\n      \"structured_vs_unstructured_gap_postprune_pp\": 38.4,\n      \"structured_vs_unstructured_gap_postsft_pp\": 14.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2 新增行: Unstructured 20% — 68.2% / 76.3% / 75.8%\",\n      \"Table 3 新增行: Unstructured — no collapse, 100 steps stable\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是median tier最关键的补充实验。Unstructured pruning确认了两个核心insights: (1) Reward-accuracy decoupling is universal（连unstructured也有reward↑ accuracy=），strengthening Claim 1; (2) Training collapse is structural-pruning-specific（unstructured无collapse），confirming the structural damage mechanism。 对Self-Healing comparison: Self-Healing用25% unstructured报告recovery——我们在20% unstructured 也看到无collapse，但accuracy仍不从GRPO获益。Paper可argue: Self-Healing的\\\"RLVR recovery\\\" 可能只是reward improvement without accuracy gain，需要replication with accuracy evaluation。\\n\\n\\nUnstructured pruning at 20%仅零化individual weights而不移除structural units——所有224个attention heads和 784个MLP groups保持intact。Post-prune 68.2%远高于structured的30%(RASP)/27%(Standard)， 因为每个结构仍有80%的weights functional，network topology完全保留。 SFT恢复到76.3%——接近unpruned(81.3%)，gap仅5pp，因为结构完整性使SFT只需微调权重而非重建功能。 GRPO关键发现：NO COLLAPSE。100步训练stable（frac_zero_std<0.35, grad_norm~5.8）， reward达到0.548（vs unpruned 0.661）。但accuracy仍不改善（76.3→75.8, Δ=-0.5pp）—— reward-accuracy decoupling在unstructured pruned model上也成立（Claim 1 strengthened）， 但没有training collapse。 这直接支持structural damage hypothesis: collapse是structural pruning的specific consequence （移除entire exploration pathways），不是pruning in general的问题。Unstructured pruning 保留了所有structural redundancy，因此GRPO可以stable训练。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SFT OOD eval (Standard 20%)\",\n    \"description\": \"Standard SFT 20% (59.29% GSM8K)在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD评估\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"standard_sft_20_math500\": 0.285,\n      \"standard_sft_20_math500_stderr\": 0.02,\n      \"standard_sft_20_humaneval\": 0.305,\n      \"standard_sft_20_humaneval_stderr\": 0.036,\n      \"unpruned_sft_math500\": 0.524,\n      \"unpruned_sft_humaneval\": 0.549,\n      \"recovery_ratio_gsm8k\": 0.73,\n      \"recovery_ratio_math500\": 0.544,\n      \"recovery_ratio_humaneval\": 0.556,\n      \"ood_degradation_pp\": 18.6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 8: OOD evaluation — Standard SFT 20% on MATH-500 (28.5%) and HumanEval (30.5%)\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OOD eval在median tier下是contingency experiment（only needed if GRPO RASP advantage <5pp， which it is: -0.84pp）。结果confirms SFT recovery的domain specificity。 Paper discussion中acknowledge: \\\"SFT recovery on in-domain data partially reconstructs task-specific patterns rather than general reasoning capability.\\\"\\n\\n\\nStandard SFT从1%(post-prune)恢复到59.29%(GSM8K)看似impressive（+58pp）， 但OOD evaluation揭示这部分recovery是GSM8K-specific。 MATH-500 28.5%（recovery ratio 54.4% vs GSM8K的73%）——MATH-500需要更复杂的 multi-step reasoning，pruning damage对这类task影响更大，且SFT on GSM8K gold 不能transfer reasoning chain construction ability to harder problems。 HumanEval 30.5%（ratio 55.6%）——code tasks需要不同的能力分布，GSM8K-specific SFT 不提供code generation ability恢复。 OOD degradation证明pruned model的SFT recovery部分是\\\"pattern reconstruction on GSM8K\\\" 而非\\\"genuine reasoning ability recovery\\\"。这为future work（multi-domain recovery data） 提供了动机。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO at 20% (re-run)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B上RASP/Standard 20%的GRPO训练，验证cross-model collapse\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_20_sft_ref\": 0.725,\n      \"standard_20_sft_ref\": 0.71,\n      \"rasp_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 12,\n      \"rasp_20_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.028,\n      \"rasp_20_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.88,\n      \"standard_20_grpo_collapse_step\": 18,\n      \"standard_20_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.045,\n      \"standard_20_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.82,\n      \"post_grpo_rasp_accuracy\": 0.718,\n      \"post_grpo_standard_accuracy\": 0.705,\n      \"collapse_ratio\": 1.5,\n      \"collapse_ratio_ci_95\": [\n        0.8,\n        2.8\n      ],\n      \"rasp_vs_standard_collapse_overlap\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5: Cross-model results — Qwen-Math-7B GRPO collapse dynamics\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-model evidence confirms Claim 1（GRPO collapse在不同model上都发生）， 但weakens Claim 2——collapse severity gradient在Qwen-Math上不clean。 Paper rewording: \\\"The collapse severity gradient is a diagnostic tendency observed on DeepSeek-R1-Distill, with directionally consistent but not statistically significant replication on Qwen2.5-Math-7B.\\\"\\n\\n\\nQwen-Math-7B与DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B虽然share Qwen2.5 backbone但training paradigm 不同——Qwen-Math是math-specific SFT，DeepSeek-R1-Distill是reasoning distillation。 两者的internal redundancy分布不同，导致RASP和Standard在Qwen-Math上的CKA-based selection differential更小。 GRPO collapse在两者上都发生（confirming Claim 1 cross-model），但RASP step 12 vs Standard step 18 的ratio仅1.5x（vs DeepSeek的6x），且95% CI [0.8, 2.8]包含1——不显著。 这是因为Qwen-Math的math-specific training使层间redundancy更均匀分布， RASP和Standard的pruning selection差异更小，导致collapse dynamics差异缩小。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Qwen-Math-7B GRPO at 25%\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-Math-7B上RASP/Standard 25%的GRPO训练\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rasp_25_sft_ref\": 0.64,\n      \"standard_25_sft_ref\": 0.63,\n      \"rasp_25_grpo_collapse_step\": 8,\n      \"rasp_25_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.015,\n      \"rasp_25_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.93,\n      \"standard_25_grpo_collapse_step\": 14,\n      \"standard_25_grpo_peak_reward\": 0.031,\n      \"standard_25_grpo_final_frac_zero_std\": 0.87,\n      \"post_grpo_rasp_accuracy\": 0.632,\n      \"post_grpo_standard_accuracy\": 0.624,\n      \"collapse_ratio\": 1.75,\n      \"collapse_ratio_ci_95\": [\n        0.9,\n        3.1\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5 新增25%行: Qwen-Math-7B 25% sparsity GRPO results\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"25% Qwen-Math结果与20%方向一致但仍not significant。 Paper conclusion: GRPO collapse is robust across models (Claim 1 strong), but the severity gradient as a diagnostic tool requires further model diversity to establish generality (Claim 2 hedged).\\n\\n25%稀疏度在Qwen-Math上进一步加速collapse：RASP step 8, Standard step 14。 Ratio从1.5(20%)略增到1.75(25%)，因为higher sparsity使differential effects marginally stronger。 但CI仍包含1——RASP vs Standard的差异在cross-model设置下not significant。 SFT gap仅1pp（64% vs 63%），进一步confirm CKA-aware selection在不同model architecture 的internal redundancy distribution下不produce consistent advantage。 两者都collapse confirms GRPO failure的robustness across models and sparsity levels。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":480,"startLine":1,"totalLines":480}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SFuKXUDmZkBV6NA9Scq2Kg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LCnU6g8EqWdJcPpePDNkqX","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/median/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11350,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11350},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48c08390-6e43-4eee-8b11-75b8377777e6","uuid":"ac832a54-3b6b-44f3-b154-934ac67a071e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LCnU6g8EqWdJcPpePDNkqX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n5\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight (Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff)\n9\tRLVR alignment (GRPO) fundamentally fails on structurally pruned reasoning models: reward improves but accuracy does not — a pruning-induced reward hacking phenomenon. We show the failure mechanism via **collapse dynamics**: pruning method determines how fast GRPO collapses, and this speed is a diagnostic of structural damage type. Crucially, functional redundancy plays **opposite roles** under SFT vs RLVR recovery:\n10\t\n11\t- **SFT**: redundant structures (high CKA overlap) are safely removable — their function redistributes through gradient-based learning. CKA-aware pruning (RASP) yields marginal SFT advantage.\n12\t- **RLVR**: redundant structures provide **exploration stability** — backup paths that prevent policy collapse during RL. Removing them (as RASP does) accelerates collapse.\n13\t\n14\tThis creates a **Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff**: the structures optimal to prune for SFT recovery are exactly those needed for RLVR stability. Optimal pruning is fundamentally conditioned on the recovery paradigm.\n15\t\n16\t## Core Claims (3) — REVISED based on experimental evidence\n17\t\n18\t1. **GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling is universal; pruning adds training collapse**: GRPO does not improve reasoning accuracy for ANY model post-SFT — unpruned (**81.27% = SFT 81.27%, Δ=0.00pp, identical 1072/1319 correct**), Standard-pruned (58.91% vs 59.29%, Δ=-0.38pp), RASP-pruned (60.65% vs 61.49%, Δ=-0.84pp). Reward increases dramatically (unpruned: 0→0.661) yet accuracy is unchanged — a universal reward-accuracy decoupling under GRPO+GSM8K+greedy. The pruning-specific phenomenon is **training collapse**: RASP collapses permanently at step ~10 (frac_zero_std→0.95, grad→0.007), Standard shows transient dip at step ~60, while unpruned trains stably for 100 steps. GRPO's reward signal does not encode genuine reasoning improvement; pruning removes the structural capacity to even sustain RL training.\n19\t\n20\t2. **Collapse severity gradient diagnoses structural damage**: Three-model comparison reveals a clean severity gradient — RASP (removes redundant, protects unique): permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039; Standard (importance-only): transient dip step ~60, final reward 0.065; Unpruned: no collapse, final reward 0.661. The 6× speedup from Standard→RASP confirms that functional redundancy provides RLVR exploration stability. Collapse dynamics are a zero-cost diagnostic: fast collapse = aggressive redundancy removal = poor RL trainability.\n21\t\n22\t3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning strategy**: For SFT recovery, RASP shows marginal advantage (+2.2pp, RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%, N=1319, p=0.25). For RLVR stability, RASP is actively harmful (6× faster collapse). The structures optimal to prune for SFT are exactly those needed for RLVR stability — a fundamental Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff. Consistent with \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" (ICLR 2026).\n23\t\n24\t## Evidence Status (as of 2026-05-16, ALL CORE DATA COMPLETE)\n25\t\n26\t| Evidence | Status | Result |\n27\t|----------|--------|--------|\n28\t| Unpruned SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 81.27% |\n29\t| Unpruned GRPO step-100 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **81.27% (Δ=0.00pp, 1072/1319 = identical to SFT)** |\n30\t| Unpruned GRPO step-90 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **80.59% (1063/1319, confirms stability across late training)** |\n31\t| Standard SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 59.29% |\n32\t| Standard GRPO step-50 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 58.91% (Δ=-0.38pp) |\n33\t| RASP SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 61.49% |\n34\t| RASP GRPO step-5 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 60.65% (Δ=-0.84pp) |\n35\t| RASP GRPO v9 collapse dynamics | ✅ | Permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039 |\n36\t| Standard GRPO v8 dynamics | ✅ | Transient dip step ~60, recovery step ~90 |\n37\t| Unpruned GRPO v2 dynamics | ✅ | No collapse, 100 steps stable, reward 0.661 |\n38\t| Alpha ablation (cal=512) | ✅ | U-shape: α≥1.0 > α≤0.5 post-prune |\n39\t| SFT gap significance | ⚠️ p=0.25 | Not significant at N=1319; scope expansion to higher sparsity planned |\n40\t| RASP GRPO step-10 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **61.87% — collapse onset does NOT reduce accuracy (vs step-5 60.65%, p=0.52)** |\n41\t\n42\t## Story Spine\n43\t\n44\t- **Problem**: The reasoning model compression pipeline (prune → recover → align) assumes alignment is independent of pruning decisions. We show this assumption fails catastrophically: GRPO alignment on pruned models produces reward improvement without accuracy gain, followed by complete collapse. The pruning-alignment interaction is not merely suboptimal — it is fundamentally broken under current practice.\n45\t\n46\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) claims RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression — but uses a single pruning ratio and does not report per-step accuracy during GRPO. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study recovery or alignment at all. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration without recovery. No work has documented GRPO collapse on pruned models, explained its mechanism, or shown that pruning strategy determines collapse dynamics.\n47\t\n48\t- **Our framing**: We present the first systematic study of how structural pruning interacts with RLVR alignment in reasoning LLMs. We introduce RASP (S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α) not as a universally superior method, but as a **diagnostic tool** that reveals the Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff: CKA-aware structure selection that benefits SFT recovery actively harms RLVR stability. This reframes the pruning-alignment relationship from \"which structures to remove for best recovery\" to \"recovery paradigm determines what counts as safe to remove.\"\n49\t\n50\t- **Headline result**: \"GRPO reward improvement never translates to accuracy gain (unpruned: reward 0→0.661, accuracy 81.27%→81.27%; identical 1072/1319 correct). But pruning causes GRPO training collapse: RASP-pruned collapses permanently at step 10, Standard-pruned at step 60, unpruned never. The severity gradient (RASP > Standard > Unpruned) reveals that structural redundancy — expendable for SFT — provides critical RL exploration stability.\"\n51\t\n52\t## Venue Fit\n53\t- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: structured pruning + reasoning model alignment failure analysis\n54\t- Negative/diagnostic results challenging published claims (Self-Healing) are high-impact at *ACL venues\n55\t- Reasoning model compression pipeline failures are immediately practical (timely: DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, Kimi-K1.5)\n56\t- Mechanistic analysis (collapse dynamics, reward-accuracy divergence) aligns with EMNLP empirical rigor\n57\t\n58\t## Venue Fit Risks\n59\t- **\"Just a negative result without solution\"**: Mitigate with (1) mechanistic explanation (redundancy-stability tradeoff), (2) RASP as diagnostic tool (collapse speed predicts pruning quality for RL), (3) actionable implication (SFT-only recovery is currently the safe path; RLVR needs pruning-aware modifications)\n60\t- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the canonical open reasoning model; multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard/Unpruned) + multi-recovery (SFT/GRPO) compensates\n61\t- **\"GRPO config might be wrong\"**: Report hyperparameter sensitivity (alpha ablation), show collapse is robust across configs, cite Self-Healing uses similar GRPO setup\n62\t- **\"SFT gap not significant\"**: Frame honestly as marginal; the paper's contribution is the GRPO failure + mechanism, not the SFT comparison. SFT gap is supplementary context.\n63\t- **\"Collapse might be training instability, not pruning-specific\"**: Unpruned GRPO ran 100 steps with zero collapse (reward 0.661, stable frac_zero_std ≤0.275) — pruning-specificity confirmed\n64\t\n65\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n66\t\n67\t| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n68\t|---------|----------|----------------------|\n69\t| GRPO failure might be hyperparameter issue | Alpha ablation shows U-shape is robust; reward increases but accuracy never follows | alpha_ablation_sweep |\n70\t| Need unpruned control for pruning-specificity | Unpruned GRPO: 100 steps stable, no collapse, reward 0.661 vs pruned collapse at step 10-60 | grpo_unpruned_v2 |\n71\t| SFT gap not significant | Acknowledged; paper's main claim is GRPO failure, not SFT superiority | sft_eval N=1319 |\n72\t| Collapse speed might not generalize | Multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard) + multi-config (alpha sweep) | grpo_v8, grpo_v9 |\n73\t| How does this relate to Self-Healing claims? | Self-Healing uses 25% unstructured; our structured pruning at 20% creates different damage pattern | Discussion section |\n74\t| What's the practical recommendation? | SFT recovery only for structurally pruned models; RLVR requires pruning-aware alignment (future work) | All experiments |\n75\t| CKA-aware pruning hurts RLVR — why publish RASP? | RASP is the diagnostic tool that REVEALS the tradeoff; its failure under RLVR is the evidence | grpo_v9 vs grpo_v8 |\n76\t\n77\t## Key Differentiations\n78\t- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: Claims RLVR recovers pruned models → we show GRPO fails (reward hacking + collapse); different pruning granularity and controlled collapse analysis\n79\t- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → we use intra-layer CKA as diagnostic tool revealing redundancy-stability tradeoff in reasoning LLMs\n80\t- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery/alignment study → we study the full prune-recover-align pipeline failure\n81\t- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → we study recovery paradigm interaction\n82\t- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → we show even optimal pruning STRUCTURE cannot save RLVR alignment\n83\t\n84\t## Open Questions (scope expansion experiments planned)\n85\t1. ~~Does unpruned model also show reward-accuracy divergence?~~ → YES, confirmed: 81.27% = 81.27%\n86\t2. ~~What do RASP v9 fine-grained checkpoints show?~~ → Permanent collapse, step-5 eval = 60.65% (≈ SFT)\n87\t3. Can higher sparsity (25-30%) make SFT gap significant AND intensify GRPO collapse? (scope expansion Phase 1)\n88\t4. Does the collapse pattern reproduce on Qwen2.5-Math-7B? (scope expansion Phase 2)\n89\t5. Is there a GRPO config that avoids collapse on pruned models? (future work motivation)\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48c08390-6e43-4eee-8b11-75b8377777e6","uuid":"757af12b-9c30-4e49-a448-3b12d1e06487","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:20:29.843Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T144805/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — recovery_aware_struct_prune\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25 submission)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026\n\n## Core Insight (Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff)\nRLVR alignment (GRPO) fundamentally fails on structurally pruned reasoning models: reward improves but accuracy does not — a pruning-induced reward hacking phenomenon. We show the failure mechanism via **collapse dynamics**: pruning method determines how fast GRPO collapses, and this speed is a diagnostic of structural damage type. Crucially, functional redundancy plays **opposite roles** under SFT vs RLVR recovery:\n\n- **SFT**: redundant structures (high CKA overlap) are safely removable — their function redistributes through gradient-based learning. CKA-aware pruning (RASP) yields marginal SFT advantage.\n- **RLVR**: redundant structures provide **exploration stability** — backup paths that prevent policy collapse during RL. Removing them (as RASP does) accelerates collapse.\n\nThis creates a **Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff**: the structures optimal to prune for SFT recovery are exactly those needed for RLVR stability. Optimal pruning is fundamentally conditioned on the recovery paradigm.\n\n## Core Claims (3) — REVISED based on experimental evidence\n\n1. **GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling is universal; pruning adds training collapse**: GRPO does not improve reasoning accuracy for ANY model post-SFT — unpruned (**81.27% = SFT 81.27%, Δ=0.00pp, identical 1072/1319 correct**), Standard-pruned (58.91% vs 59.29%, Δ=-0.38pp), RASP-pruned (60.65% vs 61.49%, Δ=-0.84pp). Reward increases dramatically (unpruned: 0→0.661) yet accuracy is unchanged — a universal reward-accuracy decoupling under GRPO+GSM8K+greedy. The pruning-specific phenomenon is **training collapse**: RASP collapses permanently at step ~10 (frac_zero_std→0.95, grad→0.007), Standard shows transient dip at step ~60, while unpruned trains stably for 100 steps. GRPO's reward signal does not encode genuine reasoning improvement; pruning removes the structural capacity to even sustain RL training.\n\n2. **Collapse severity gradient diagnoses structural damage**: Three-model comparison reveals a clean severity gradient — RASP (removes redundant, protects unique): permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039; Standard (importance-only): transient dip step ~60, final reward 0.065; Unpruned: no collapse, final reward 0.661. The 6× speedup from Standard→RASP confirms that functional redundancy provides RLVR exploration stability. Collapse dynamics are a zero-cost diagnostic: fast collapse = aggressive redundancy removal = poor RL trainability.\n\n3. **Recovery method conditions optimal pruning strategy**: For SFT recovery, RASP shows marginal advantage (+2.2pp, RASP 61.49% vs Standard 59.29%, N=1319, p=0.25). For RLVR stability, RASP is actively harmful (6× faster collapse). The structures optimal to prune for SFT are exactly those needed for RLVR stability — a fundamental Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff. Consistent with \"RL Squeezes, SFT Expands\" (ICLR 2026).\n\n## Evidence Status (as of 2026-05-16, ALL CORE DATA COMPLETE)\n\n| Evidence | Status | Result |\n|----------|--------|--------|\n| Unpruned SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 81.27% |\n| Unpruned GRPO step-100 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **81.27% (Δ=0.00pp, 1072/1319 = identical to SFT)** |\n| Unpruned GRPO step-90 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **80.59% (1063/1319, confirms stability across late training)** |\n| Standard SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 59.29% |\n| Standard GRPO step-50 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 58.91% (Δ=-0.38pp) |\n| RASP SFT eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 61.49% |\n| RASP GRPO step-5 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | 60.65% (Δ=-0.84pp) |\n| RASP GRPO v9 collapse dynamics | ✅ | Permanent collapse step ~10, peak reward 0.039 |\n| Standard GRPO v8 dynamics | ✅ | Transient dip step ~60, recovery step ~90 |\n| Unpruned GRPO v2 dynamics | ✅ | No collapse, 100 steps stable, reward 0.661 |\n| Alpha ablation (cal=512) | ✅ | U-shape: α≥1.0 > α≤0.5 post-prune |\n| SFT gap significance | ⚠️ p=0.25 | Not significant at N=1319; scope expansion to higher sparsity planned |\n| RASP GRPO step-10 eval (N=1319) | ✅ | **61.87% — collapse onset does NOT reduce accuracy (vs step-5 60.65%, p=0.52)** |\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: The reasoning model compression pipeline (prune → recover → align) assumes alignment is independent of pruning decisions. We show this assumption fails catastrophically: GRPO alignment on pruned models produces reward improvement without accuracy gain, followed by complete collapse. The pruning-alignment interaction is not merely suboptimal — it is fundamentally broken under current practice.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-Healing (2025) claims RLVR recovers pruned reasoning models to 95%+ at 25% compression — but uses a single pruning ratio and does not report per-step accuracy during GRPO. GRASPrune (ACL 2026) provides SOTA budgeted structural pruning but doesn't study recovery or alignment at all. RESP (Dec 2025) uses reasoning-trace calibration without recovery. No work has documented GRPO collapse on pruned models, explained its mechanism, or shown that pruning strategy determines collapse dynamics.\n\n- **Our framing**: We present the first systematic study of how structural pruning interacts with RLVR alignment in reasoning LLMs. We introduce RASP (S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α) not as a universally superior method, but as a **diagnostic tool** that reveals the Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff: CKA-aware structure selection that benefits SFT recovery actively harms RLVR stability. This reframes the pruning-alignment relationship from \"which structures to remove for best recovery\" to \"recovery paradigm determines what counts as safe to remove.\"\n\n- **Headline result**: \"GRPO reward improvement never translates to accuracy gain (unpruned: reward 0→0.661, accuracy 81.27%→81.27%; identical 1072/1319 correct). But pruning causes GRPO training collapse: RASP-pruned collapses permanently at step 10, Standard-pruned at step 60, unpruned never. The severity gradient (RASP > Standard > Unpruned) reveals that structural redundancy — expendable for SFT — provides critical RL exploration stability.\"\n\n## Venue Fit\n- EMNLP Efficient Methods track: structured pruning + reasoning model alignment failure analysis\n- Negative/diagnostic results challenging published claims (Self-Healing) are high-impact at *ACL venues\n- Reasoning model compression pipeline failures are immediately practical (timely: DeepSeek-R1, QwQ, Kimi-K1.5)\n- Mechanistic analysis (collapse dynamics, reward-accuracy divergence) aligns with EMNLP empirical rigor\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **\"Just a negative result without solution\"**: Mitigate with (1) mechanistic explanation (redundancy-stability tradeoff), (2) RASP as diagnostic tool (collapse speed predicts pruning quality for RL), (3) actionable implication (SFT-only recovery is currently the safe path; RLVR needs pruning-aware modifications)\n- **\"Single model\"**: DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B is the canonical open reasoning model; multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard/Unpruned) + multi-recovery (SFT/GRPO) compensates\n- **\"GRPO config might be wrong\"**: Report hyperparameter sensitivity (alpha ablation), show collapse is robust across configs, cite Self-Healing uses similar GRPO setup\n- **\"SFT gap not significant\"**: Frame honestly as marginal; the paper's contribution is the GRPO failure + mechanism, not the SFT comparison. SFT gap is supplementary context.\n- **\"Collapse might be training instability, not pruning-specific\"**: Unpruned GRPO ran 100 steps with zero collapse (reward 0.661, stable frac_zero_std ≤0.275) — pruning-specificity confirmed\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Experimental Responses\n\n| Concern | Response | Supporting Experiment |\n|---------|----------|----------------------|\n| GRPO failure might be hyperparameter issue | Alpha ablation shows U-shape is robust; reward increases but accuracy never follows | alpha_ablation_sweep |\n| Need unpruned control for pruning-specificity | Unpruned GRPO: 100 steps stable, no collapse, reward 0.661 vs pruned collapse at step 10-60 | grpo_unpruned_v2 |\n| SFT gap not significant | Acknowledged; paper's main claim is GRPO failure, not SFT superiority | sft_eval N=1319 |\n| Collapse speed might not generalize | Multi-method comparison (RASP/Standard) + multi-config (alpha sweep) | grpo_v8, grpo_v9 |\n| How does this relate to Self-Healing claims? | Self-Healing uses 25% unstructured; our structured pruning at 20% creates different damage pattern | Discussion section |\n| What's the practical recommendation? | SFT recovery only for structurally pruned models; RLVR requires pruning-aware alignment (future work) | All experiments |\n| CKA-aware pruning hurts RLVR — why publish RASP? | RASP is the diagnostic tool that REVEALS the tradeoff; its failure under RLVR is the evidence | grpo_v9 vs grpo_v8 |\n\n## Key Differentiations\n- **vs Self-Healing (2025)**: Claims RLVR recovers pruned models → we show GRPO fails (reward hacking + collapse); different pruning granularity and controlled collapse analysis\n- **vs MPruner (2024)**: inter-layer CKA for depth pruning in CNNs → we use intra-layer CKA as diagnostic tool revealing redundancy-stability tradeoff in reasoning LLMs\n- **vs GRASPrune (ACL 2026)**: SOTA budgeted pruning without recovery/alignment study → we study the full prune-recover-align pipeline failure\n- **vs RESP (Dec 2025)**: reasoning-trace calibration without recovery → we study recovery paradigm interaction\n- **vs PASER (2025)**: optimizes recovery DATA → we show even optimal pruning STRUCTURE cannot save RLVR alignment\n\n## Open Questions (scope expansion experiments planned)\n1. ~~Does unpruned model also show reward-accuracy divergence?~~ → YES, confirmed: 81.27% = 81.27%\n2. ~~What do RASP v9 fine-grained checkpoints show?~~ → Permanent collapse, step-5 eval = 60.65% (≈ SFT)\n3. Can higher sparsity (25-30%) make SFT gap significant AND intensify GRPO collapse? (scope expansion Phase 1)\n4. Does the collapse pattern reproduce on Qwen2.5-Math-7B? (scope expansion Phase 2)\n5. Is there a GRPO config that avoids collapse on pruned models? (future work motivation)\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FwzH6PjQh4GD59JvtBvTxQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have all the information I need to write the paper. Let me organize the key data points:\n\n**Experiment data summary:**\n1. Post-prune baselines N=1319 (20%): RASP 29.8%, Standard 26.1%, Unpruned 85.4%\n2. All recovered models: RASP SFT 61.49%, Standard SFT 59.29%, Unpruned SFT 81.27%, Unpruned GRPO 81.27% (Δ=0.00pp), RASP GRPO -0.84pp, Standard GRPO -0.38pp, GRASPrune SFT 39.5%, GRASPrune GRPO 38.8%\n\n\n3. GRASPrune's full pipeline shows post-prune performance at 6.8%, recovering to 39.5% with SFT before collapsing at step 18 during GRPO training\n4. Multi-seed results confirm robustness with RASP at 30.4±2.8% and Standard at 26.5±3.2% (p=0.024), and the scoring ablation reveals RASP's superiority over gradient-based and magnitude-based approaches\n5. CKA analysis indicates moderate recoverability overall (r=0.38) with weaker within-layer alignment (r=0.22) but strong layer-level consistency (ICC=0.71)\n6. SFT-only baseline shows RASP maintaining a 2.2 percentage point advantage over Standard (61.49% vs 59.29%), though this gap isn't statistically significant (p=0.25), while higher sparsity levels reveal RASP's earlier collapse at 25% sparsity compared to Standard's more gradual degradation\n7. Extended evaluation across diverse benchmarks shows MATH-500 at 31.8%, HumanEval at 35.4%, and MMLU at 51.2%, with Bonsai demonstrating similar collapse patterns and CKA reliability metrics confirming consistency across split-half validation (ρ=0.93)\n8. The alpha sensitivity analysis shows a U-shaped relationship with optimal performance at α=2.0, while unstructured pruning surprisingly avoids collapse entirely, achieving 76.3% accuracy with SFT and maintaining a reward of 0.548 despite only a 0.5 percentage point accuracy drop\n9. Cross-model validation on Qwen-Math-7B reveals RASP collapses roughly 1.5-1.75x faster than Standard across both 20% and 25% sparsity levels, though confidence intervals include 1, and inference speedup reaches approximately 15% latency reduction at 20% sparsity\n10. The three main claims are that GRPO exhibits universal failure under pruning, collapse severity varies across models but the gradient weakens in cross-model settings, and the redundancy-stability tradeoff is an empirical observation rather than a fundamental principle—with unstructured pruning serving as the critical baseline for validating the structural damage hypothesis\n11. Now I'm writing the full LaTeX paper with sections for abstract, introduction, related work, methods, comprehensive experiments, discussion, and conclusion, ensuring each experiment gets its own table and narrative treatment.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16649,"cache_read_input_tokens":23191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16649},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48c08390-6e43-4eee-8b11-75b8377777e6","uuid":"fa336239-9c90-4293-b369-bc79568c4616"}
